<title>UK: Yorkshire B/S adds 50 million marks to 7-year FRN.</title>
<headline>Yorkshire B/S adds 50 million marks to 7-year FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate has</p>
<p>been increased to 200 million marks from 150 million marks lead</p>
<p>manager UBS Frankfurt said on Friday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   YORKSHIRE BUILDING SOCIETY</p>
<p> AMT   *200 MLN DEM   BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY    11.AUG.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     +10 BP    PAY DATE    11.AUG.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A2	  ISS PRICE  100.042   FULL FEES   20 BP</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 100	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  UK	  TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    10 BP     SELL CONC  10 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	*LAUNCHED ORIGINALLY FOR 150 MLN MARKS ON 24.JUL.97.</p>
<p>		 ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
